From c4d8ce87530f37976b7295d8e43e872b33e6ef43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaming Zhang <772577952@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:53:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kasan: implement kernel address sanitizer support

Add KASAN=1 error detection support for Asterinas v0.19.0.

Implement boot-time 4-level zero-page shadow hierarchy in bsp_boot.S,
dynamic shadow memory mapping in ostd::mm::kspace, comprehensive KASAN
runtime ABI in ostd::kasan (loads/stores, memory intrinsics, reports,
globals and noreturn handling) marked with #[sanitize(address = "off")],
slab/heap allocator hooks in ostd::mm::heap to poison redzones and
freed memory, and intrusive freelist traversal exemptions in slot_list.

Update Makefile and tools/kcov-rustc.sh to support an independent 4-state
matrix across KCOV and KASAN, maintaining zero-sancov in ostd and
applying -Cunsafe-allow-abi-mismatch=sanitizer across target crates.
